  "open_questions": [
    "The two spaces between LEO and Earth Escape carry a small red rocket icon. What does it mean?",
    "Hatched grey bars (LEO to Escape) are not in the legend. Plain burn, or something else?",
    "Earth Escape is marked with a diamond, not a dot. Can you park there?",
    "GEO forks off the second rocket-icon space, so LEO to GEO = 3 dv, the same as Escape (real: ~3.9 vs ~3.2 km/s). Intended?",
    "Mars descent has 4 crossings (so ascent = 4, matching docs/04), but docs/04 says descent = 3 propulsive / 1 with heatshield. Transcribed as: first crossing a burn, the 3 red-hatched ones free with Atmospheric Return (= 1 dv aerobraked, 4 propulsive). Docs call the red hatch 'purely aesthetic'. Which is right?",
    "Parking assumed on every deep-space and Mars-route space (coasting counts as parked). The board has no markers there.",
    "LEO has no dot but is surely a parking orbit.",
    "Stray marks on the PDF: a pale blue disc left of Earth, a lone green dashed bar under the Mars route, a small empty square bottom-right. Leftovers?",
    "Board routes check out against docs/04 except the Mars descent (4 crossings vs 3 in the docs). Lunar orbit -> Mars orbit is 6 dv fast / 4 slow; docs/04's '4' is the slow route."
  ]
